"""Day-6 tape selector over the 58-tape rating-3029 cluster.

Every tape in the cluster has byte-identical field actions for days 0-5, so at
step 144 any of them can be spliced in losslessly (verified: A->B reproduces B
alone to the dollar). That makes step 144 the one real decision point, and the
per-world oracle over it is worth about $18k a game above the best fixed tape.

The source agent does NOT do this: across 58 episodes with 58 seeds, 34 distinct
day-6 shop pairs and 23 opponents it plays days 0-5 identically, and its later
branching does not track the shop draw. So this conditions on something the
recorded play never used.

Rule: a yarn store among the first two shops means wool demand is real all
season (YARN_STORE is the ONLY consumer of wool, and it takes 12 units a day),
which rewards a different continuation than a world without one.
"""
